msgid "Web dependency locator"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This document shows how static resources can be served from web dependency "
"jars like https://www.webjars.org[WebJars] and https://mvnpm.org[mvnpm]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using the <code>quarkus-web-dependency-locator</code> extension"
msgstr ""

msgid "WebJars"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are using https://www.webjars.org[WebJars], like the following JQuery "
"one:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"you can reference the files in the jar from your HTML, example `/webjars/"
"jquery/3.1.1/jquery.min.js`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The above is available by default, however, adding the `{web-locator-ga}` "
"extension allows you to reference the files without having to include the "
"version in the path, example `/webjars/jquery/jquery.min.js`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mvnpm"
msgstr ""

msgid "If you are using https://mvnpm.org[mvnpm], like the following Lit one:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"you can reference the files in the jar from your HTML, example `/_static/lit/"
"3.1.2/index.js`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The above is available by default, however, adding the `{web-locator-ga}` "
"extension allows you to reference the files without having to include the "
"version in the path, example `/_static/lit/index.js`."
msgstr ""

msgid "ImportMaps"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mvnpm jars also allows you to use an https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/"
"docs/Web/HTML/Element/script/type/importmap[importmap], that will\n"
"allow you to just use module imports, example `import { LitElement, html, "
"css} from 'lit';`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The importmap is generated by the `{web-locator-ga}` extension, and "
"available at `/_importmap/generated_importmap.js`.\n"
"This means adding the following to your `index.html` will allow you to "
"import web libraries by name:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the generated importmap"
msgstr ""

msgid "Import web libraries"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Import your own files, this can be done by adding `quarkus.web-dependency-"
"locator.import-mappings.app/ = /app/` to the config. Any key-value pair can "
"be added."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic imports"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can also automate the imports above. To do this, move your web assets "
"from `src/main/resources/META-INF/resources` to `src/main/resources/web`\n"
"and now replace the above scripts and imports with `{#bundle /}`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This will be replaced at build time with the importmap script, and also "
"include any CSS and JavaScript discovered in the `/app` directory."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This allows you to add libraries, js and css without having to change your "
"HTML. Hot-reload is also supported."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When adding the `{web-locator-ga}` extension , you can see the files being "
"served, and the generated importmap, in the Dev UI:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"image:web-dependency-locator-screenshot01.png[alt=Card in Dev UI]\n"
"image:web-dependency-locator-screenshot02.png[alt=Files]\n"
"image:web-dependency-locator-screenshot03.png[alt=Importmap]"
msgstr ""
